(window.DVR_PAPERS=window.DVR_PAPERS||{})["da-easy-2025-006"]={"v":1,"id":"da-easy-2025-006","title":"Basic Level Test-2 Full Syllabus GATE 2025 DA","sourceTitle":"Basic Level Test-2 Full Syllabus GATE 2025 DA","branch":"DATA SCIENCE AND ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE","code":"DA","provider":"DVRUO EASY","providerKey":"easy","series":"GATE 2025 Online Test Series - Data Science and AI","seriesId":"da-easy-2025","num":6,"category":"basic","year":"2025","format":"A","durationSec":10800,"info":{"meta":"Package: GATE 2026 + GATE 2025 Online Test Series - Data Science and AI • Questions: 65","package":"GATE 2026 + GATE 2025 Online Test Series - Data Science and AI"},"source":"DATA SCIENCE AND ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE/MADE EASY/GATE_2026_+_GATE_2025_Online_Test_Series_Data_Science_and_AI/011_Basic Level Test-2 Full Syllabus GATE 2025 DA.html","questions":[{"n":1,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • INSTRUMENTATION ENGINEERING • Beginner • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\tA train travels at a original speed for a distance of 63 km and then travels a distance of 72 km at an average speed of 6 km/hr more than its original speed. If it takes 3 hours to complete the total journey, what is the original speed of the train in km/hr?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"24"},{"key":"B","html":"33"},{"key":"C","html":"42"},{"key":"D","html":"66"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(c)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/55/55ae6043d80cdd78b224.png\" /></p>"},{"n":2,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • INSTRUMENTATION ENGINEERING • Beginner • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>\n\t60 g of sugar was mixed in 360 <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/e6/e62d91ecc27b75309c5b.png\" /> water in a vessel <em>A</em>, 80 g of sugar was mixed in 560 ml of water in vessel <em>B</em> and 40 g of sugar was mixed in 200 ml of water in vessel <em>C</em>. The solution in vessel <em>B</em> is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\tSweeter than that in <em>C</em></p>"},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\tSweeter than that in <em>A</em></p>"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\tAs sweet as that in <em>C</em></p>"},{"key":"D","html":"<p>\n\tLess sweet than that in <em>C</em></p>"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>\n\t(d)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/23/2308a74a98efe2fd5cb1.png\" /></p>"},{"n":3,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • INSTRUMENTATION ENGINEERING • Beginner • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\tThe two pie charts below show the percentage market share on value basis of the companies <em>A</em> to <em>E</em> in a sectorial market for 1999 and 2000.</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6b/6b3bcaaeed2ea629b770.png\" /></p>\n<p>\n\tWhich company had the minimum growth rate in sales in these two years?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"B"},{"key":"B","html":"A"},{"key":"C","html":"D"},{"key":"D","html":"E"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(b)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1f/1fdd233972ddd280f2f8.png\" /></p>"},{"n":4,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • INSTRUMENTATION ENGINEERING • Beginner • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>\n\tA survey was conducted on a sample of 1000 persons with reference to their knowledge of English, French and German. The results of the survey are presented in the given Venn diagram. The ratio of the number of persons who do not know any of the three languages to those who know all the three languages is</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b4/b4364e862a0e86056305.png\" /></p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ed/ed6fd08515fea8c8fe66.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/7e/7e7ca4bbbd81bef9700b.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/45/458d11cdfad5feffc347.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"D","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/54/54c31e54b81fe989f29e.png\" /></p>"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>\n\t(b)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/99/99486bba1570258f6a68.png\" /></p>"},{"n":5,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • INSTRUMENTATION ENGINEERING • Beginner • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>\n\tIn how many maximum different ways can 3 identical balls be placed in the 12 squares (each ball to be placed in the exact centre of the squares and only one ball is to be placed in one square) shown in the figure given below such that they do not lie along the same straight line?</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1a/1a63868364e38916772a.png\" /></p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"144"},{"key":"B","html":"204"},{"key":"C","html":"200"},{"key":"D","html":"216"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>\n\t(c)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/7e/7ec690b9cb45ba6798c9.png\" /></p>"},{"n":6,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • INSTRUMENTATION ENGINEERING • Beginner • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\tIn a code language, ‘SOLID’ is written as ‘WPSLPIMFHA’, what does the code ‘ATEXXQIBVO’ refer to?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"EAGER"},{"key":"B","html":"WAFER"},{"key":"C","html":"WAGER"},{"key":"D","html":"WATER"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(d)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/da/dabcc927b5ea178c4218.png\" /></p>"},{"n":7,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • INSTRUMENTATION ENGINEERING • Beginner • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>\n\tLooking into a mirror, the analog clock shows 9 : 30 as the time. The actual time is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"2 : 30"},{"key":"B","html":"3 : 30"},{"key":"C","html":"4 : 30"},{"key":"D","html":"6 : 30"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>\n\t(a)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b2/b2da5148020800d06130.png\" /></p>"},{"n":8,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • INSTRUMENTATION ENGINEERING • Beginner • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\tWhich of phrases given below should replace the phrase printed in bold type to make it grammatically correct?<br />\n\t<strong>Despite of their</strong> differences on matters of the principles, they all agree on the demand of hike in salary.</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Despite their"},{"key":"B","html":"Despite of them"},{"key":"C","html":"Despite for their"},{"key":"D","html":"Despite off their"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(a)<br />\n\t&ldquo;Despite their&rdquo; in place of &ldquo;Despite of their&rdquo;. The preposition &quot;of&quot; is unnecessary after &quot;despite&quot;.</p>"},{"n":9,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • INSTRUMENTATION ENGINEERING • Beginner • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\tChoose an option, which can be substituted for the given phrase:<br />\n\tSomething that can not be imitated.</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Inimitable"},{"key":"B","html":"Inevitable"},{"key":"C","html":"Duplicity"},{"key":"D","html":"Inexplicable"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(a)<br />\n\tInimitable means incapable of being duplicated. The word duplicity means dishonest behavior that is intended to trick someone. Something that is impossible to explain is called inexplicable and something that is impossible to avoid or prevent is termed as inevitable.</p>"},{"n":10,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • INSTRUMENTATION ENGINEERING • Beginner • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>\n\tRatio of perimeter of circumscribed circle to inscribed circle about a square is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/03/032439a70837913390ae.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"B","html":"2"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b8/b82f4355e326f6f6c337.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"D","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/52/52a95a3b9c6e03550c08.png\" /></p>"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>\n\t(a)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/77/77c3cb9964fda7f37fe0.png\" /></p>"},{"n":11,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tThe probability of getting at least 3 consecutive tails in 4 tosses of a fair coin is equal to _______.<br />\n\t(Upto 2 decimal places)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.18,0.2],"answerText":"0.18 [0.18 - 0.20]","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t0.18 [0.18 - 0.20]</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/50/5028eabaca3058400e8e.png\" /></p>"},{"n":12,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tLet A be a 3 × 3 matrix with rank 2. Then AX = 0 has</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"The trivial solution X = 0."},{"key":"B","html":"One independent solution."},{"key":"C","html":"Two independent solutions."},{"key":"D","html":"Three independent solutions."}],"answer":["A","B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t(a, b)<br />\n\tIf r is the rank of matrix A and n &times; n is the order of matrix then we shall have (n &ndash; r) linearly independent non-trivial solutions. Any linear combination of these (n &ndash; r) solutions will also be a solution of AX = 0.</p>"},{"n":13,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>\n\tConsider the following Python Code:</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d9/d9533787044b6efcd5ea.png\" /></p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"25 15 35"},{"key":"B","html":"15 25"},{"key":"C","html":"15 16 35"},{"key":"D","html":"26 37 48"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>\n\t(b)<br />\n\tThe function with static variable &lsquo;fun.i&rsquo; that retains its value across call, and a local variable &lsquo;j&rsquo; that reinitialized each time. In two calls, &lsquo;fun.i&rsquo; starts at 1 and is incremented with each call, while j is always 5.<br />\n\tOutput will be 15 25.</p>"},{"n":14,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\tThe density function of the time between arrival of buses is given by <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/23/23bfd20d5b2aac2ad20b.png\" /> is the time in minutes. What is the probability that the time between arrival is less than 5 minutes?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"0"},{"key":"B","html":"1"},{"key":"C","html":"2"},{"key":"D","html":"3"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(b)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f6/f67b17096e24b19cbc55.png\" /></p>\n<p>\n\t&nbsp;</p>"},{"n":15,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tThe value of <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/30/30e93561d5f08acdb3d7.png\" /> will be ________. (Upto 2 decimal places)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.5,0.5],"answerText":"0.5 [0.50 - 0.50]","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t0.5 [0.50 - 0.50]</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a1/a15e34a5f569a8bc2a2e.png\" /></p>"},{"n":16,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tConsider the following Python code:</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/dd/dd11e749fdd82e64b34e.png\" /></p>\n<p>\n\tWhat will be the output of the above code?</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[1025,1025],"answerText":"1025","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t1025</p>"},{"n":17,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\tIn the context of decision trees, the Gini index is preferred over entropy when:<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>1</sub> : The dataset is large and efficiency is a concern.<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>2</sub> : The focus is on maximizing information gain.<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>3</sub> : There are many categorical features with high cardinality.</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\tOnly <em>S</em><sub>1</sub></p>"},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\tOnly <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p>"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\tBoth <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p>"},{"key":"D","html":"None of these"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(a)<br />\n\tThe Gini index is often preferred over entropy for efficiency reasons, especially with large datasets. Entropy focuses on maximizing information gain, which is not directly related to the choice of the Gini index.</p>"},{"n":18,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\tConsider the following statements:<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>1</sub> : Systematic sampling requires a randomly chosen starting point and a fixed periodic interval for selecting subsequent samples.<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>2</sub> : Systematic sampling can lead to biased results if the population has a hidden pattern related to the sampling interval.<br />\n\tWhich of the above is true?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\tOnly <em>S</em><sub>1</sub></p>"},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\tOnly <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p>"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\tBoth <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p>"},{"key":"D","html":"None of these"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(c)<br />\n\t&bull; Systematic sampling, a randomly chosen starting point is selected, followed by sampling at regular intervals (e.g., every k<sup>th</sup> element). So, <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> is correct.<br />\n\t&bull; Systematic sampling can lead to biased results if there is a hidden pattern or cyclical nature in the population that aligns with the sampling interval. So, <em>S</em><sub>2</sub> is incorrect.</p>"},{"n":19,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\tConsider the following statements:<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>1</sub> : Spanned strategy suitable for variable length records.<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>2</sub> : In the spanned strategy, a record can span multiple blocks.<br />\n\tWhich of the above is correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\tOnly <em>S</em><sub>1</sub></p>"},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\tOnly <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p>"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\tBoth <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p>"},{"key":"D","html":"None of these"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(c)<br />\n\t&bull; Spanned strategy a record can span across multiple blocks if the record size exceeds the block size.<br />\n\t&bull; Spanned strategy suitable for variable length records because it allows records to be divided and stored across multiple blocks when they don&rsquo;t fit in a single block.</p>"},{"n":20,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tLet A be the result when the postfix expression below in evaluated.</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ea/ea98c6f484a31ec86e26.png\" /></p>\n<p>\n\tThen the value of <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/ea/eab7db625ddd1497a072.png\" /> will be ________. (Upto 1 decimal place)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[26.6,26.6],"answerText":"26.6 [26.6 - 26.6]","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t26.6 [26.6 - 26.6]</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f6/f65699a1bdd128f2dc8b.png\" /></p>"},{"n":21,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tThe number of novels launched worldwide in a month follows Poisson distribution with mean(μ) as 5.2. The probability of launching less than 3 novels in a randomly selected month is _______. (Upto 2 decimal places)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.1,0.11],"answerText":"0.10 [0.10 - 0.11]","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t0.10 [0.10 - 0.11]</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/36/360a0924a003d518a5e1.png\" /></p>"},{"n":22,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\tWhich of the following statements is correct?<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>1</sub> : The trace of square matrix <em>A</em> has sum of diagonal element.<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>2</sub> : The transpose of square matrix <em>A</em> has the same Eigen values as those of <em>A</em>.</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\tOnly <em>S</em><sub>1</sub></p>"},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\tOnly <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p>"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\tBoth <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p>"},{"key":"D","html":"None of these"}],"answer":["A","C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C, A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(c)<br />\n\t&bull; Trace (<em>A</em>) = Sum of diagonal<br />\n\t&bull; Eigen value of <em>A</em> and its transpose are the same.</p>"},{"n":23,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tNiraj (<em>N</em>) can solve 70% of problems given in book and Venkatesh (<em>X</em>) can solve 60% of the problems. A problem selected at random from a book. Find the probability that the problem is solved.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.88,0.89],"answerText":"0.88 [0.88 - 0.89]","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t0.88 [0.88 - 0.89]</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b9/b98b85627f4acad429ca.png\" /></p>"},{"n":24,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\tMatch the items in <strong>Column-I</strong> with the items in <strong>Column-II</strong> in the following table:</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/8d/8d162d5d93edcd35a822.png\" /></p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"a"},{"key":"B","html":"b"},{"key":"C","html":"c"},{"key":"D","html":"d"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(b)<br />\n\t&bull; Decision Tree &rarr; Discriminative Model<br />\n\t&bull; Principal Component Analysis &rarr; Dimensionality Reduction<br />\n\t&bull; Gaussian Mixture Model &rarr; Generative Model</p>"},{"n":25,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\tMatch the items in <strong>Column-I</strong> with the items in <strong>Column-II</strong> in the following table:</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c8/c8e2260e58cf9f18ca6b.png\" /></p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"a"},{"key":"B","html":"b"},{"key":"C","html":"c"},{"key":"D","html":"d"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(a)<br />\n\t&bull; Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP) &rarr; Feed Forward Architecture<br />\n\t&bull; Bias-Variance Trade-Off &rarr; Trade-off in Model Complexity<br />\n\t&bull; Decision Tree &rarr; Hierarchical Decision Making<br />\n\t&bull; Cross-Validation &rarr; Data Resampling Technique</p>"},{"n":26,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\tConsider the following statements:<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>1</sub> : On any random input insertion sort is work more efficiently than bubble sort.<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>2</sub> : Average number of comparison of insertion sort is better than bubble sort by constant factor. If efficiency, is considered as number of comparison to sort an array [input], then which of the<br />\n\tfollowing is correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\tOnly <em>S</em><sub>1</sub></p>"},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\tOnly <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p>"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\tBoth <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p>"},{"key":"D","html":"<p>\n\tNeither <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> nor <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p>"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(b)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b5/b5e356d04284f38bd12a.png\" /></p>"},{"n":27,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tConsider a relation <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/1b/1b2be3ea0547e710e60b.png\" /> with primary key P, R and U respectively.<br />\n\tAssume that <em>r</em><sub>1</sub> has 200 tuples, <em>r</em><sub>2</sub> has 125 tuples and <em>r</em><sub>3 </sub>has 85 tuples. The number of resultant tupple in <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/d4/d442a6b51db39affebd6.png\" /> are ________.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[17000,17000],"answerText":"17000","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t17000</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f0/f031fff0009d6807bbdf.png\" /></p>"},{"n":28,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\tThe players <em>A</em>, <em>B</em> and <em>C</em> toss an unbiased coin in sequence, starting with <em>A</em>, then <em>B</em> and then <em>C</em>. The first player to get head wins the game. What is the probability that <em>B</em> wins the game?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/71/71119621246ec06f37e0.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/08/0846ad0bfbf68b791aee.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a0/a0d5bf1c1ae5fe999e4c.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"D","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/10/10e882f9392fb1f7a5b4.png\" /></p>"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(b)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5e/5e855b2f150cd12da36b.png\" /></p>"},{"n":29,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\tWhat will be the out of the program:</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/30/307e2c0424c7445ef98f.png\" /></p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"5, 4, 3, 2, 1"},{"key":"B","html":"1, 2, 3, 4, 5"},{"key":"C","html":"5, 4, 3, 2, 1, 0"},{"key":"D","html":"Infinite loop"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(a)<br />\n\tHere reverse function prints the current value of num and recursively calls itself with num &ndash; 1 until num reaches 0. For each recursive call, it prints num before making the next call. The base as termination the recursion without printing, the output 5, 4, 3, 2, 1.</p>"},{"n":30,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\tConsider a schema <em>R</em>(<em>P</em>, <em>Q</em>, <em>R</em>, <em>S</em>, <em>T</em>, <em>U</em>) and functional dependencies:</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b5/b51c07b5521ea65c1744.png\" /></p>\n<p>\n\tThe decomposition of R into <em>R</em><sub>1</sub>(<em>PQST</em>), <em>R</em><sub>2</sub>(<em>PQR</em>) and <em>R</em><sub>3</sub>(<em>TU</em>) is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Lossless join and dependency preserving."},{"key":"B","html":"Lossless join but not dependency preserving."},{"key":"C","html":"Lossy join but dependency preserving."},{"key":"D","html":"Neither lossless join nor dependency preserving."}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(a)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/14/1465e96303b8336e94fd.png\" /></p>"},{"n":31,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>\n\tWhich of the following statements is/are correct?<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>1</sub> : Ridge regression can be used to improve the performance of a linear regression model by adding a penalty term.<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>2</sub> : K-means clustering is used to fit a linear model to the data.<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>3</sub> : K-means clustering requires specifying the number of clusters before the algorithm starts.</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\tOnly <em>S</em><sub>1</sub></p>"},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\tOnly <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p>"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\tOnly <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>3</sub></p>"},{"key":"D","html":"<p>\n\tOnly <em>S</em><sub>2</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>3</sub></p>"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>\n\t(c)<br />\n\t&bull; Ridge regression adds a penalty term (L2 regularization) to the linear regression model to reduce overfitting and improve performance by shrinking the coefficients. So, <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> is correct.<br />\n\t&bull; K-means clustering is a method for partitioning data into clusters based on similarity, not for fitting a linear model. So, <em>S</em><sub>2</sub> is incorrect.<br />\n\t&bull; K-means clustering requires the number of clusters (<em>k</em>) to be specified before running the algorithm. So, <em>S</em><sub>3</sub> is correct.</p>"},{"n":32,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\tConsider the following statements:<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>1</sub>  : Alpha-beta pruning is applied after evaluating every node in the Mini-Max tree.<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>2</sub> : The Mini-Max algorithm with alpha-beta pruning can be significantly faster than the standard Mini-Max algorithm due to reduced branching.<br />\n\tWhich of the above statements is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\tOnly <em>S</em><sub>1</sub></p>"},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\tOnly <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p>"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\tBoth <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p>"},{"key":"D","html":"None of these"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(b)<br />\n\t&bull; Alpha-beta pruning is applied during the evaluation of nodes, not after evaluating every node. So, <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> is incorrect.<br />\n\t&bull; Alpha-beta pruning can make the Mini-Max algorithm significantly faster by reducing the number of nodes evaluated through pruning. So, <em>S</em><sub>2</sub> is correct.</p>"},{"n":33,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tIf <em>A</em> is non-singular matrix, then possible value of <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/5b/5b4e798113753c81c79c.png\" /> is</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4b/4b67c6ebc3061c7b5552.png\" /></p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[3,3],"answerText":"3","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t3</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/13/13c8a3f8eb764c15cd3f.png\" /></p>"},{"n":34,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0","html":"<p>\n\t<img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/59/59282505700283ce324c.png\" /> is equal to ________.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[8,8],"answerText":"8","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t8</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/26/268be2d67280b9e16b8c.png\" /></p>"},{"n":35,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tA node in a decision tree contains 200 samples, with 120 samples in Class <em>X</em> and 80 samples in Class <em>Y</em>. If the node is split into two child nodes based on a feature, with the following distribution: Left Child Node: 100 samples (70 in Class <em>X</em>, 30 in Class <em>Y</em>) and Right Child Node: 100 samples (50 in Class <em>X</em>, 50 in Class <em>Y</em>), calculate the Gini Index for the left child node.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.42,0.42],"answerText":"0.42","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t0.42</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/44/445e685eaeba04fa21bd.png\" /></p>"},{"n":36,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tWhich of the following statements is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\tDFT takes Ο(V<sup>2</sup>) time in a graph G(V, E) if graph is represent with adjacent matrix.</p>"},{"key":"B","html":"For a directed graph, the absence of back edges in a DFT tree means graph as no cycle."},{"key":"C","html":"DFT can be implemented using queue data structure."},{"key":"D","html":"<p>\n\tBFT takes Ο(V<sup>3</sup>) time in a graph G(V, E) if graph is represent with adjacent list.</p>"}],"answer":["A","B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t(a, b)<br />\n\t&bull; DFT and BFT take &Omicron;(V<sup>2</sup>) using adjacent matrix.<br />\n\t&bull; DFT can be implemented using stack data structure.</p>"},{"n":37,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tConsider the Set <em>A</em> = {1, 2, 3, ..... 1}. Two elements <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/3a/3a276bba60120ec52f00.png\" /> and ‘y’ are chosen at random from set. The probability that element chosen satisfy <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/6c/6c8811dc210f7166005f.png\" />= 14 is equal to ________. [Upto 2 decimal places]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.05,0.05],"answerText":"0.05","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t0.05</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5b/5bfa76de468746608150.png\" /></p>"},{"n":38,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tWhich of the following statements is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Support Vector Machines (SVM) use kernel functions to map data into higher dimensions for separation."},{"key":"B","html":"Leave-One-Out (LOO) cross-validation uses each sample as a separate test set."},{"key":"C","html":"SVM is used for dimensionality reduction."},{"key":"D","html":"LOO cross-validation is computationally less intensive than k-fold cross-validation."}],"answer":["A","B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t(a, b)<br />\n\t&bull; SVMs use kernel functions to map data into higher dimensions to find a separating hyperplane<br />\n\twhen data is not linearly separable. So, option (a) is correct.<br />\n\t&bull; LOO cross-validation uses each sample as a test set and the rest as the training set, repeating<br />\n\tthis process for each sample. So, option (b) is correct.<br />\n\t&bull; SVM is used for classification and regression, not for dimensionality reduction. So, option (c) is incorrect.<br />\n\t&bull; LOO cross-validation is more computationally intensive than k-fold cross-validation because it requires training the model n times (for each sample). So, option (d) is incorrect.</p>"},{"n":39,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tConsider the following ERD:</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/7d/7d3500e8342fb14848ee.png\" /></p>\n<p>\n\tThe number of minimum Relations which satisfy 1NF _________. (Partial participation between <em>E</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>R</em> should not lost in R DBMS design).</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[2,2],"answerText":"2","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t2</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fc/fc85fa0b1ad4bedfb986.png\" /></p>"},{"n":40,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>\n\tFind the worst case time complexity of the following recurrence relations:</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f9/f98c2b674aca8b7839bc.png\" /></p>\n<p>\n\twhere c is a constant and <em>T</em>(2) = 1</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\tΩ(log<sub>2</sub> log<sub>2</sub> <em>n</em>)</p>"},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\tΩ(log2 n)</p>"},{"key":"C","html":"Ω(n)"},{"key":"D","html":"<p>\n\tΩ(n log<sub>2</sub> n)</p>"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>\n\t(a)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ec/ec6839572cee79cfd5d1.png\" /></p>"},{"n":41,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/9c/9c13218f520eb7b54b55.png\" /></p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"779"},{"key":"B","html":"679"},{"key":"C","html":"0"},{"key":"D","html":"1"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>\n\t(c)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/bb/bb2dd34c3bf0c924f324.png\" /></p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a2/a22f8f97ffb1739b8689.png\" /></p>"},{"n":42,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tConsider <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/4c/4c8b7793ececa51d3d95.png\" /> be a function defined by</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/67/67303b5ceb12eef978dd.png\" /></p>\n<p>\n\tIn <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/21/216a8f1d0eb790802c52.png\" /> exist, then the value of <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/7f/7fd676a227f5fe249fac.png\" /> is ________.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[-1,-1],"answerText":"-1","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t-1</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/34/3404490326d8e73f88c4.png\" /></p>"},{"n":43,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>\n\tWhich of the following statements is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Linear Discriminant Analysis (LDA) is used for dimensionality reduction by maximizing class separability."},{"key":"B","html":"Ridge regression is used to reduce the dimensionality of data."},{"key":"C","html":"LDA is suitable for binary classification problems."},{"key":"D","html":"Ridge regression involves transforming data into principal components."}],"answer":["A","B","C","D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, B, C, D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>\n\t(a)<br />\n\t&bull; LDA aims to reduce dimensionality while maximizing the separation between classes. It projects data onto a lower-dimensional space in a way that enhances class separability. So, option (a) is correct.<br />\n\t&bull; Ridge regression is a technique used to handle multi-collinearity by adding a penalty term to the regression coefficients, but it does not reduce dimensionality. It addresses overfitting by shrinking the coefficients. So, option (b) is incorrect.<br />\n\t&bull; LDA can be used for both binary and multiclass classification problems. It&rsquo;s not limited to binary classification. So, option (c) is incorrect.<br />\n\t&bull; Ridge regression does not involve transforming data into principal components. It adds a penalty to the regression coefficients to reduce overfitting, whereas Principal Component Analysis (PCA) is used for dimensionality reduction by transforming data into principal components. So, option (d) is incorrect.</p>"},{"n":44,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>\n\tConsider the following statements:<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>1</sub> : Rejection sampling involves accepting samples from a proposal distribution based on their likelihood of matching the target distribution.<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>2</sub> : Gibbs sampling is an MCMC method that samples from conditional distributions iteratively to approximate a multivariate distribution.<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>3</sub> : The Gini index quantifies distribution inequality by comparing the area between the Lorenz curve and the line of equality.<br />\n\tWhich of the following statements is correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\tOnly <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p>"},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\tOnly <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>3</sub></p>"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\tOnly <em>S</em><sub>2</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>3</sub></p>"},{"key":"D","html":"None of these"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>\n\t(c)<br />\n\t&bull; Rejection sampling uses a likelihood ratio to decide whether to accept or reject samples, not just accepting based on likelihood alone. So, <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> is incorrect.<br />\n\t&bull; Gibbs sampling is indeed an MCMC method for generating samples by iterating through conditional distributions. So, <em>S</em><sub>2</sub> is correct.<br />\n\t&bull; The Gini index measures inequality by comparing the area between the Lorenz curve and the equality line. So, <em>S</em><sub>3</sub> is correct.</p>"},{"n":45,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>\n\tWhat will be the output of the following Python code:</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/db/db460c4ecad2609044c4.png\" /></p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"15, 20, 25, 25"},{"key":"B","html":"15, 20, 25, 30"},{"key":"C","html":"15, 20, 15, 15"},{"key":"D","html":"15, 15, 20, 20"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>\n\t(c)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a7/a7e874d781bca3f6a316.png\" /></p>"},{"n":46,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tIf <em>P</em> and <em>Q</em> are two random events, then which of the following is false?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\tIndependence of <em>P</em> and <em>Q</em> implies that probability (<em>P</em> ∩ <em>Q</em>) = 0</p>"},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\tProbability (<em>P</em> ∪ <em>Q</em>) ≥ Probability (<em>P</em>) + Probability (<em>Q</em>)</p>"},{"key":"C","html":"If P and Q are mutually exclusive, then they must be independent."},{"key":"D","html":"<p>\n\tProbability (<em>P</em> ∩ <em>Q</em>) ≤ Probability (<em>P</em>)</p>"}],"answer":["A","B","C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, B, C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t(a, b, c)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/33/333d302d4d3677ea14ee.png\" /></p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/bd/bd89261f00080c34df68.png\" /></p>"},{"n":47,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\tConsider the following schema and given SQL query:<br />\n\tproduct (product_Id, category, price)<br />\n\tSelect distinct P.product_Id<br />\n\tFROM product P, Product Q<br />\n\tWHERE P.price < Q.price<br />\n\tAND Q.category = “Electronics”<br />\n\tWhich of the following is returned by the above SQL query?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Product IDs of any product that costs less than all product in the Electronics category."},{"key":"B","html":"Product IDs of all product that cost less than atleast one product in the Electronics category."},{"key":"C","html":"Product IDs of all distinct products that cost less than all products in the Electronics category."},{"key":"D","html":"None of these"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(b)<br />\n\tSQL query returns the product IDs of all product that cost less than atleast one product in the Electronics category.</p>"},{"n":48,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>\n\tIf the density function of a continuous random variable <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/35/35bc77c99983738ef62b.png\" /> is given by</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/99/994f0615037dff0d12e2.png\" /></p>\n<p>\n\tFind the value of <em>b</em></p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/37/376617f7a83536fe21d0.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f5/f5ef6a33ba830c138c94.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/79/797755c21a8f3983e1b8.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"D","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/45/455ba3cfc4f69db77600.png\" /></p>"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>\n\t(c)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a0/a0031d9a799cebec6f99.png\" /></p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fc/fc37be67d3782bc38a4d.png\" /></p>"},{"n":49,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>\n\tWhich of the following statements is/are true?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"The R-squared value in Linear Regression indicates the proportion of variance explained by the model."},{"key":"B","html":"Decision Trees use only the mean squared error for splitting nodes in classification tasks."},{"key":"C","html":"K-means clustering algorithm operates based on hierarchical clustering principles."},{"key":"D","html":"Support Vector Machines (SVM) are primarily used for clustering tasks."}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>\n\t(a)<br />\n\t&bull; R-squared indicates the proportion of variance in the dependent variable explained by the model. So, option (a) is correct.<br />\n\t&bull; Decision Trees can use various criteria for splitting nodes, not limited to mean squared error.<br />\n\tSo, option (b) is incorrect.<br />\n\t&bull; K-means clustering is not hierarchical; it partitions data into k clusters. So, option (c) is incorrect.<br />\n\t&bull; SVMs are primarily used for classification and regression, not clustering. So, option (d) is incorrect.</p>"},{"n":50,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>\n\tConsider the following statements:<br />\n\t(a) Cluster sampling is preferred over simple random sampling when the population is heterogeneous within clusters.<br />\n\t(b) Clusters should be as homogenous as possible to minimize sampling error.<br />\n\t(c) Cluster sampling provides more precision than stratified sampling.<br />\n\t(d) In cluster sampling, smaller clusters generally lead to more accurate results.<br />\n\tWhich of the above statements is correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"a"},{"key":"B","html":"b"},{"key":"C","html":"c"},{"key":"D","html":"d"}],"answer":["A","B","C","D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B, A, C, D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>\n\t(b)<br />\n\t&bull; Cluster sampling is preferred when there is heterogeneity between clusters and homogeneity within clusters. This ensures that the sample is representative. So, option (a) is incorrect.<br />\n\t&bull; Clusters as homogeneous as possible reduces the variability within clusters, which helps minimize sampling error. So, option (b) is correct.<br />\n\t&bull; Cluster sampling typically provides less precision than stratified sampling, especially when there is high within-cluster similarity. So, option (c) is incorrect.<br />\n\t&bull; Size of clusters alone does not guarantee more accurate results; it&rsquo;s the representativeness and structure of the clusters that matter more. Smaller clusters do not necessarily lead to better accuracy. So, option (d) is incorrect.</p>"},{"n":51,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tIf matrix <em>A</em> = <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/39/392dd9b35a8ea61cb011.png\" /> then the possible eigen vectors for the matrix <em>A</em> are:</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/30/30a2b369551def5484ca.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/0f/0fdbac6b2dd8f39a229d.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a6/a6e10f1a2cce1152a295.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"D","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e6/e6a7ae40e4e6b2ce7e7a.png\" /></p>"}],"answer":["A","B","C","D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, B, C, D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t(a, b, c, d)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b9/b9001d669866fd5b2f18.png\" /></p>"},{"n":52,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tConsider <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/1d/1d1c00df85bf5e6f4b26.png\" /> The minimum value of <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/56/56ea90164fecb7d7d8dc.png\" /> over the interval [0, 2] is ________.<br />\n\t(Upto 1 decimal place)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[6,6],"answerText":"6","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t6</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d6/d68b52c4ae4f66ddee09.png\" /></p>"},{"n":53,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tConsider the already built heap (max heap):<br />\n\t34, 30, 26, 18, 22, 20, 25, 16, 1<br />\n\tHow many number of element the leaf node after 2 deletions?</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[4,4],"answerText":"4","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t4</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4c/4c6f39accaa3cbbf60aa.png\" /></p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a8/a85c2426fade8f7d59d8.png\" /></p>"},{"n":54,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tA company tracks the average monthly sales of its product and finds that the average sales over 12 months is $ 1200. If the sales for the 13<sup>th</sup> months are $ 1500. What is the updated average sales? (Upto 2 decimal)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[1223,1223.09],"answerText":"1223.07 [1223.0 - 1223.09]","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t1223.07 [1223.0 - 1223.09]</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/01/01d97f7b559fc992a42a.png\" /></p>"},{"n":55,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\tA is an involutory matrix given by <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/64/640aeaf49f0b9aab908d.png\" /> then the inverse of <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/7f/7fae29adbfbeffde0432.png\" /> will be</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\t1<em>A</em></p>"},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c7/c7ee0d7b6728bf0d42d0.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/86/864e3d40bfe63d472f57.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"D","html":"<p>\n\t2<em>A</em></p>"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(d)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/29/2985968da09510493e66.png\" /></p>"},{"n":56,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>\n\tLet square(<img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/70/70291acfbec8795c882a.png\" />): <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/70/70291acfbec8795c882a.png\" /> is a square; white(<img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/70/70291acfbec8795c882a.png\" />): <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/70/70291acfbec8795c882a.png\" /> is white; empty(<img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/70/70291acfbec8795c882a.png\" />, <em>t</em>): <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/70/70291acfbec8795c882a.png\" /> is empty at time <em>t</em>.<br />\n\tConsider the sentence S as “White squares are always empty”. Now consider the following first order logic sentences.</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b0/b0684bb7df38cc80202b.png\" /></p>\n<p>\n\tWhich of the above are correct first order logic translations of S?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Only I"},{"key":"B","html":"Only II"},{"key":"C","html":"Both I and II"},{"key":"D","html":"None of these"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>\n\t(c)<br />\n\tBoth are correct translations of the sentence S.<br />\n\tHence (c) is correct.</p>"},{"n":57,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tConsider the following statements:<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>1</sub> : Every directed acyclic graph has exactly one topological ordering.<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>2</sub> : Dijkstra’s algorithm may not terminate if graph contains negative weight edges.<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>3</sub> : If load factor of a hash table is less than 1, then there are no collision.<br />\n\tThe number of statements correct are __________.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0,0],"answerText":"0","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t0</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4b/4b9048b57729cd699998.png\" /></p>"},{"n":58,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tThe maximum number of BFS traversal possible on Binary Search Tree of height 3 ________.<br />\n\t(Assume root is at height 0)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[128,128],"answerText":"128","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t128</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5f/5f3cd913b9327d5b0cb6.png\" /></p>"},{"n":59,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>\n\t<img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/d4/d40a2a97247016af0ee7.png\" /></p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"0"},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/94/94a2c1024f90339bc5e8.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c9/c9aaacf43c6b7dcba82e.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"D","html":"1"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>\n\t(b)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6f/6f61d90033f887927c68.png\" /></p>"},{"n":60,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tSelect all the correct statements:</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Quick sort has combine step of divide and conquer technique."},{"key":"B","html":"Merge sort always has more number of swaps that comparisons."},{"key":"C","html":"Number of comparisons in partition algorithm are same for best case and worst case."},{"key":"D","html":"Quick sort is an inplace algorithm while merge sort is an out place algorithm."}],"answer":["B","C","D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B, C, D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t(b, c, d)<br />\n\t(a) Quick sort only has divide step and conquer step.<br />\n\t(b) True: Since merge sort is an out place algorithm.<br />\n\t(c) True: Number of comparisons in partition algorithm do not change for best case or worst case.<br />\n\t(d) True</p>"},{"n":61,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tWhich of the following statement false about B tree and B<sup>+</sup> tree index? Assume order of B tree node same as order of B<sup>+</sup> tree node.</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\tB tree index has more levels than B<sup>+</sup> tree index for large number of keys.</p>"},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\tB<sup>+</sup> tree index has more levels than B tree index for large number of keys.</p>"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\tBoth B tree B<sup>+</sup> tree best for sequential access of records.</p>"},{"key":"D","html":"<p>\n\tB tree index nodes more than B<sup>+</sup> tree for large number of keys.</p>"}],"answer":["A","C","D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, C, D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t(a, c, d)<br />\n\tB<sup>+</sup> tree index has more levels than B-tree index for large number of keys. Since in B-tree every key appears at only single level but which is not the case for B<sup>+</sup> tree.</p>"},{"n":62,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>\n\tConsider two well formed formulas in propositional logic:</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/54/544394407076a721a8f2.png\" /></p>\n<p>\n\tWhich of the following is correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\t<em>F</em><sub>1</sub> is satisfiable, <em>F</em><sub>2</sub> is valid</p>"},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\t<em>F</em><sub>1</sub> is unsatisfiable, <em>F</em><sub>2</sub> is satisfiable</p>"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\t<em>F</em><sub>1</sub> is unsatisfiable, <em>F</em><sub>2</sub> is valid</p>"},{"key":"D","html":"<p>\n\t<em>F</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>F</em><sub>2</sub> both are unsatisfiable</p>"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>\n\t(b)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/90/902500261fda2274a509.png\" /></p>"},{"n":63,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tConsider the following graph and sequences given below:</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ef/efefc928d1c5bccf58a8.png\" /></p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b1/b10a8a59fb4eb5812fa1.png\" /></p>\n<p>\n\tThe number of sequences are BFS traversal on the given graph __________.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[2,2],"answerText":"2","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t2</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/41/414307fd51f1056010e3.png\" /></p>"},{"n":64,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>\n\tIn a Binomial distribution, the mean is 12 and variance is 3. Find the value of <em>P</em>(probability of success) and n(total number of trails).</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a4/a475d9d987f9141296a5.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"B","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/3a/3a3d917bc86e8800e1fa.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"C","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/69/691e303ed4acecf4ccba.png\" /></p>"},{"key":"D","html":"<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/23/23eaea49ddf42288d979.png\" /></p>"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>\n\t(c)</p>\n<p>\n\t<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/02/02769371d1be5d28668e.png\" /></p>"},{"n":65,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0","html":"<p>\n\tConsider the following statements:<br />\n\t(a) In two-stage cluster sampling, the second stage always involves selecting all elements from each selected cluster.<br />\n\t(b) Cluster sampling can be combined with stratified sampling to improve accuracy.<br />\n\t(c) Cluster sampling is ideal when the population consists of geographically dispersed group.<br />\n\t(d) Cluster sampling tends to give smaller standard errors compared to simple random sampling.<br />\n\tWhich of the above statements is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"a"},{"key":"B","html":"b"},{"key":"C","html":"c"},{"key":"D","html":"d"}],"answer":["B","C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B, C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>\n\t(b, c)<br />\n\t(a) In two-stage cluster sampling, not all elements in selected clusters are always sampled; often, only a subset is chosen. So, option (a) is incorrect.<br />\n\t(b) Cluster sampling can be combined with stratified sampling to improve accuracy by ensuring that different strata are well-represented within clusters. So, option (b) is correct.<br />\n\t(c) Cluster sampling is ideal for geographically dispersed populations because it reduces logistical challenges and costs. So, option (c) is correct.<br />\n\t(d) Cluster sampling generally results in larger standard errors compared to simple random sampling due to higher within-cluster similarity. So, option (d) is incorrect.</p>"}],"math":false,"scoring":"marks","sections":[{"name":"General Aptitude","start":0,"count":10},{"name":"Technical","start":10,"count":55}],"stats":{"questions":65,"maxMarks":100,"types":{"MCQ":35,"NAT":19,"MSQ":11},"withoutKey":0}};
